{"id":"mahabharata-8-023","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":23,"title":"त्रयोविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 23 · Duryodhana asks Shalya to drive Karna's chariot","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana humbly asks the king of Madra to be Karna's charioteer, and Shalya, angered, refuses, saying he will not be a sutaputra's driver. After Duryodhana's coaxing and praise, Shalya agrees on condition that he may speak freely.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ವಿನಯದಿಂದ ಮದ್ರರಾಜನನ್ನು ಕರ್ಣನ ಸಾರಥಿಯಾಗಲು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ಶಲ್ಯ ಸೂತಪುತ್ರನ ಸಾರಥಿಯಾಗೆನೆಂದು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಒಲೈಕೆ, ಹೊಗಳಿಕೆಯ ನಂತರ ಮುಕ್ತವಾಗಿ ಮಾತನಾಡಬಹುದೆಂಬ ಷರತ್ತಿನ ಮೇಲೆ ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन विनम्रता से मद्रराज से कर्ण का सारथी बनने को कहता है, और क्रुद्ध शल्य सूतपुत्र का सारथी बनने से मना करता है। दुर्योधन की मनुहार और प्रशंसा के बाद शल्य खुलकर बोलने की शर्त पर मान जाता है।","te":"దుర్యోధనుడు వినయంగా మద్రరాజును కర్ణునికి సారథిగా ఉండమని కోరతాడు; కోపించిన శల్యుడు సూతపుత్రునికి సారథిని కానని తిరస్కరిస్తాడు. దుర్యోధనుని బుజ్జగింపు, పొగడ్తల తరువాత స్వేచ్ఛగా మాట్లాడవచ్చనే షరతుపై అంగీకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"துரியோதனன் பணிவுடன் மத்ர மன்னனைக் கர்ணனின் தேரோட்டியாகக் கேட்க, சினமுற்ற சல்யன் சூதன் மகனுக்குத் தேரோட்டியாகேன் என்று மறுக்கிறான். துரியோதனனின் இனிய சொற்களுக்குப்பின் வெளிப்படையாகப் பேசலாம் என்ற நிபந்தனையுடன் ஒப்புகிறான்.","ml":"കർണ്ണന്റെ രഥം ഓടിക്കണമെന്ന് മദ്രരാജാവായ ശല്യനോട് ദുര്യോധനൻ വിനയത്തോടെ അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; സൂതപുത്രന്റെ സാരഥിയാകില്ലെന്ന് പറഞ്ഞ് ശല്യൻ കോപത്തോടെ വിസമ്മതിക്കുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനന്റെ നിർബന്ധത്തിനും പ്രശംസയ്ക്കും ശേഷം, സ്വതന്ത്രമായി സംസാരിക്കാൻ അനുവദിക്കണമെന്ന ഉപാധിയോടെ ശല്യൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.23; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुत्रस्तव महाराज मद्रराजमिदं वचः ।\nविनयेनोपसंगम्य प्रणयाद्वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, your son approached the king of the Madras with humility and, in friendship, spoke these words."}},{"n":2,"text":"सत्यव्रत महाभाग द्विषतामघवर्धन ।\nमद्रेश्वर रणे शूर परसैन्यभयंकर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Man of true vows, greatly blessed, increaser of your enemies' sorrow, lord of the Madras, hero in battle, terror of enemy armies,"}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रुतवानसि कर्णस्य ब्रुवतो वदतां वर ।\nयथा नृपतिसिंहानां मध्ये त्वां वरयत्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"best of speakers, you have heard Karna say how he chooses you from among these lion-like kings."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्मात्पार्थविनाशार्थं हितार्थं मम चैव हि ।\nसारथ्यं रथिनां श्रेष्ठ सुमनाः कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, best of chariot-warriors, for the destruction of Partha and for my good, you should gladly act as his charioteer."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्याभीशुग्रहो लोके नान्योऽस्ति भवता समः ।\nस पातु सर्वतः कर्णं भवान्ब्रह्मेव शंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no one in the world equal to you at holding the reins. As Brahma guarded Shankara, so you should guard Karna on all sides."}},{"n":6,"text":"पार्थस्य सचिवः कृष्णो यथाभीशुग्रहो वरः ।\nतथा त्वमपि राधेयं सर्वतः परिपालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Krishna, Partha's counsellor, is the best of rein-holders, so you too should protect Radha's son everywhere."}},{"n":7,"text":"भीष्मो द्रोणः कृपः कर्णो भवान्भोजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nशकुनिः सौबलो द्रौणिरहमेव च नो बलम् ।\nएषामेव कृतो भागो नवधा पृतनापते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Karna, you, the mighty Bhoja, Shakuni son of Subala, Drona's son and I myself were our strength. Among these alone, O lord of the army, our force was divided into nine shares."}},{"n":8,"text":"नैव भागोऽत्र भीष्मस्य द्रोणस्य च महात्मनः ।\nताभ्यामतीत्य तौ भागौ निहता मम शत्रवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was no share here for Bhishma and the great Drona; yet beyond those two shares, my enemies were killed by those two."}},{"n":9,"text":"वृद्धौ हि तौ नरव्याघ्रौ छलेन निहतौ च तौ ।\nकृत्वा नसुकरं कर्म गतौ स्वर्गमितोऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two tigers among men were old, and they were killed by a trick. Having done deeds not easy to do, they have gone from here to heaven, O blameless one."}},{"n":10,"text":"तथान्ये पुरुषव्याघ्राः परैर्विनिहता युधि ।\nअस्मदीयाश्च बहवः स्वर्गायोपगता रणे ।\nत्यक्त्वा प्राणान्यथाशक्ति चेष्टाः कृत्वा च पुष्कलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other tigers among men were likewise slain in battle by the enemy, and many of ours went to heaven in the fight, giving up their lives, having done all they could and much besides."}},{"n":11,"text":"कर्णो ह्येको महाबाहुरस्मत्प्रियहिते रतः ।\nभवांश्च पुरुषव्याघ्र सर्वलोकमहारथः ।\nतस्मिञ्जयाशा विपुला मम मद्रजनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna alone, the long-armed, is devoted to our welfare, and so are you, tiger among men, great chariot-warrior of all the worlds. In him and you, lord of the Madras, my hope of victory is vast."}},{"n":12,"text":"पार्थस्य समरे कृष्णो यथाभीशुवरग्रहः ।\nतेन युक्तो रणे पार्थो रक्ष्यमाणश्च पार्थिव ।\nयानि कर्माणि कुरुते प्रत्यक्षाणि तथैव ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Krishna is the best holder of the reins for Partha in battle, so you are for Karna. With him, and protected by him, Partha does the deeds you see with your own eyes."}},{"n":13,"text":"पूर्वं न समरे ह्येवमवधीदर्जुनो रिपून् ।\nअहन्यहनि मद्रेश द्रावयन्दृश्यते युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before, Arjuna did not kill enemies in battle like this. Day after day, lord of the Madras, he is seen routing them in the fight."}},{"n":14,"text":"भागोऽवशिष्टः कर्णस्य तव चैव महाद्युते ।\nतं भागं सह कर्णेन युगपन्नाशयाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The share that remains is Karna's and yours, O radiant one. Destroy that share, together with Karna, at once in the battle."}},{"n":15,"text":"सूर्यारुणौ यथा दृष्ट्वा तमो नश्यति मारिष ।\nतथा नश्यन्तु कौन्तेयाः सपाञ्चालाः ससृञ्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As darkness vanishes when Surya and Aruna are seen, so let the sons of Kunti, with the Panchalas and Srinjayas, vanish."}},{"n":16,"text":"रथानां प्रवरः कर्णो यन्तॄणां प्रवरो भवान् ।\nसंनिपातः समो लोके भवतोर्नास्ति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna is the best of chariot-warriors and you are the best of charioteers. No pairing in the world is equal to the two of you."}},{"n":17,"text":"यथा सर्वास्ववस्थासु वार्ष्णेयः पाति पाण्डवम् ।\nतथा भवान्परित्रातु कर्णं वैकर्तनं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Vrishni's son protects the Pandava in every state, so should you protect Karna, son of Vikartana, in battle."}},{"n":18,"text":"त्वया सारथिना ह्येष अप्रधृष्यो भविष्यति ।\nदेवतानामपि रणे सशक्राणां महीपते ।\nकिं पुनः पाण्डवेयानां मातिशङ्कीर्वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"With you as his charioteer he will be unassailable even by the gods with Shakra, O lord of the earth, let alone by the sons of Pandu. Do not doubt my words."}},{"n":19,"text":"दुर्योधनवचः श्रुत्वा शल्यः क्रोधसमन्वितः ।\nत्रिशिखां भ्रुकुटीं कृत्वा धुन्वन्हस्तौ पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Duryodhana's words, Shalya, filled with anger, drew his brows into three lines and shook his hands again and again."}},{"n":20,"text":"क्रोधरक्ते महानेत्रे परिवर्त्य महाभुजः ।\nकुलैश्वर्यश्रुतिबलैर्दृप्तः शल्योऽब्रवीदिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Turning his large eyes, red with anger, the long-armed Shalya, proud of his lineage, power, learning and strength, said this."}},{"n":21,"text":"अवमन्यसे मां गान्धारे ध्रुवं मां परिशङ्कसे ।\nयन्मां ब्रवीषि विस्रब्धं सारथ्यं क्रियतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son of Gandhari, you insult me, surely, and you doubt me, when you confidently tell me, 'Be the charioteer.'"}},{"n":22,"text":"अस्मत्तोऽभ्यधिकं कर्णं मन्यमानः प्रशंससि ।\nन चाहं युधि राधेयं गणये तुल्यमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"You praise Karna, thinking him greater than us, but I do not count Radha's son as equal to myself in battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"आदिश्यतामभ्यधिको ममांशः पृथिवीपते ।\nतमहं समरे हत्वा गमिष्यामि यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Assign me a greater share, lord of the earth. I will kill the enemy in battle and go back as I came."}},{"n":24,"text":"अथ वाप्येक एवाहं योत्स्यामि कुरुनन्दन ।\nपश्य वीर्यं ममाद्य त्वं संग्रामे दहतो रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or, joy of the Kurus, I will fight alone. Watch my valor today as I burn the enemy in battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"न चाभिकामान्कौरव्य विधाय हृदये पुमान् ।\nअस्मद्विधः प्रवर्तेत मा मा त्वमतिशङ्किथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man like me, Kaurava, does not act with desires set in his heart for others' wishes. Do not doubt me too much."}},{"n":26,"text":"युधि चाप्यवमानो मे न कर्तव्यः कथंचन ।\nपश्य हीमौ मम भुजौ वज्रसंहननोपमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I must never be insulted in battle. Look at these two arms of mine, like thunderbolts in their solidity."}},{"n":27,"text":"धनुः पश्य च मे चित्रं शरांश्चाशीविषोपमान् ।\nरथं पश्य च मे कॢप्तं सदश्वैर्वातवेगितैः ।\nगदां च पश्य गान्धारे हेमपट्टविभूषिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See my bow, variegated, and my arrows like venomous snakes. See my chariot, well fitted with good horses swift as the wind. And see my mace, son of Gandhari, adorned with gold plates."}},{"n":28,"text":"दारयेयं महीं क्रुद्धो विकिरेयं च पर्वतान् ।\nशोषयेयं समुद्रांश्च तेजसा स्वेन पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"In anger I could split the earth, scatter mountains and dry up the oceans by my own power, O king."}},{"n":29,"text":"तन्मामेवंविधं जानन्समर्थमरिनिग्रहे ।\nकस्माद्युनक्षि सारथ्ये न्यूनस्याधिरथेर्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing that I am such a man, able to subdue enemies, why do you set me to be charioteer for the son of Adhiratha, who is lesser than I, king?"}},{"n":30,"text":"न नाम धुरि राजेन्द्र प्रयोक्तुं त्वमिहार्हसि ।\nन हि पापीयसः श्रेयान्भूत्वा प्रेष्यत्वमुत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should not appoint me to the pole of the chariot, O best of kings. Having been better than one who is worse, I do not choose to be his servant."}},{"n":31,"text":"यो ह्यभ्युपगतं प्रीत्या गरीयांसं वशे स्थितम् ।\nवशे पापीयसो धत्ते तत्पापमधरोत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who in friendship puts a greater man, who has come under his protection, under the control of a lesser, commits a sin, high and low turned upside down."}},{"n":32,"text":"ब्राह्मणा ब्रह्मणा सृष्टा मुखात्क्षत्रमथोरसः ।\nऊरुभ्यामसृजद्वैश्याञ्शूद्रान्पद्भ्यामिति श्रुतिः ।\nतेभ्यो वर्णविशेषाश्च प्रतिलोमानुलोमजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins were created by Brahma, the Kshatriya from his chest, he made the Vaishyas from his thighs and the Shudras from his feet, so scripture says, and from them come the special classes born in reverse and direct order."}},{"n":33,"text":"अथान्योन्यस्य संयोगाच्चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य भारत ।\nगोप्तारः संग्रहीतारो दातारः क्षत्रियाः स्मृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O Bharata, by mixing among them the four classes arose, and Kshatriyas are remembered as protectors, gatherers and givers."}},{"n":34,"text":"याजनाध्यापनैर्विप्रा विशुद्धैश्च प्रतिग्रहैः ।\nलोकस्यानुग्रहार्थाय स्थापिता ब्रह्मणा भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins were placed on earth by Brahma for the good of the world, with sacrificing for others, teaching, and the acceptance of pure gifts."}},{"n":35,"text":"कृषिश्च पाशुपाल्यं च विशां दानं च सर्वशः ।\nब्रह्मक्षत्रविशां शूद्रा विहिताः परिचारकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Farming, herding and giving are the Vaishyas' tasks everywhere. Shudras are appointed as servants of Brahmins, Kshatriyas and Vaishyas."}},{"n":36,"text":"ब्रह्मक्षत्रस्य विहिताः सूता वै परिचारकाः ।\nन विट्शूद्रस्य तत्रैव शृणु वाक्यं ममानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charioteers are appointed as servants of Brahmins and Kshatriyas, not of Vaishyas and Shudras. Listen to my word, blameless one."}},{"n":37,"text":"सोऽहं मूर्धावसिक्तः सन्राजर्षिकुलसंभवः ।\nमहारथः समाख्यातः सेव्यः स्तव्यश्च बन्दिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am an anointed king, born in a family of royal sages, called a great chariot-warrior, one to be served and praised by bards."}},{"n":38,"text":"सोऽहमेतादृशो भूत्वा नेहारिकुलमर्दन ।\nसूतपुत्रस्य संग्रामे सारथ्यं कर्तुमुत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Being such a man, crusher of enemy families, I do not choose to serve here as charioteer to a charioteer's son in battle."}},{"n":39,"text":"अवमानमहं प्राप्य न योत्स्यामि कथंचन ।\nआपृच्छ्य त्वाद्य गान्धारे गमिष्यामि यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having met with this insult, I will not fight in any way. Taking leave of you, son of Gandhari, I will go back as I came.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा नरव्याघ्रः शल्यः समितिशोभनः ।\nउत्थाय प्रययौ तूर्णं राजमध्यादमर्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Shalya, tiger among men, ornament of assemblies, rose and quickly set out from the middle of the king's company, offended."}},{"n":41,"text":"प्रणयाद्बहुमानाच्च तं निगृह्य सुतस्तव ।\nअब्रवीन्मधुरं वाक्यं साम सर्वार्थसाधकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Out of affection and great respect, your son held him back and spoke gentle words, conciliating and accomplishing every aim."}},{"n":42,"text":"यथा शल्य त्वमात्थेदमेवमेतदसंशयम् ।\nअभिप्रायस्तु मे कश्चित्तं निबोध जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What you say, Shalya, is surely so, without doubt. But I have a purpose in mind, lord of men. Understand it."}},{"n":43,"text":"न कर्णोऽभ्यधिकस्त्वत्तः शङ्के नैव कथंचन ।\nन हि मद्रेश्वरो राजा कुर्याद्यदनृतं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not in any way think Karna greater than you. The king of the Madras would never do anything untrue."}},{"n":44,"text":"ऋतमेव हि पूर्वास्ते वहन्ति पुरुषोत्तमाः ।\nतस्मादार्तायनिः प्रोक्तो भवानिति मतिर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your forebears, best of men, carried truth alone. Hence I think you are called Artayani."}},{"n":45,"text":"शल्यभूतश्च शत्रूणां यस्मात्त्वं भुवि मानद ।\nतस्माच्छल्येति ते नाम कथ्यते पृथिवीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"And because you, giver of honor, are a thorn to enemies on earth, you are called Shalya, lord of the earth."}},{"n":46,"text":"यदेव व्याहृतं पूर्वं भवता भूरिदक्षिण ।\nतदेव कुरु धर्मज्ञ मदर्थं यद्यदुच्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever you said before, O giver of great gifts, do just that, knower of dharma, and whatever I tell you for my sake."}},{"n":47,"text":"न च त्वत्तो हि राधेयो न चाहमपि वीर्यवान् ।\nवृणीमस्त्वां हयाग्र्याणां यन्तारमिति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radha's son is not stronger than you, nor am I. We choose you as the driver of the best horses in the battle."}},{"n":48,"text":"यथा ह्यभ्यधिकं कर्णं गुणैस्तात धनंजयात् ।\nवासुदेवादपि त्वां च लोकोऽयमिति मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the world considers Karna better than Dhananjaya in qualities, dear friend, so it considers you better even than Vasudeva."}},{"n":49,"text":"कर्णो ह्यभ्यधिकः पार्थादस्त्रैरेव नरर्षभ ।\nभवानप्यधिकः कृष्णादश्वयाने बले तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna is superior to Partha in weapons, bull among men, and you are superior to Krishna in driving horses and in strength."}},{"n":50,"text":"यथाश्वहृदयं वेद वासुदेवो महामनाः ।\nद्विगुणं त्वं तथा वेत्थ मद्रराज न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As great-minded Vasudeva knows the hearts of horses, you know them twice as well, king of the Madras, without doubt.\""}},{"text":"शल्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shalya said:"}},{"n":51,"text":"यन्मा ब्रवीषि गान्धारे मध्ये सैन्यस्य कौरव ।\nविशिष्टं देवकीपुत्रात्प्रीतिमानस्म्यहं त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Gandhari, Kaurava, since you tell me in the middle of the army that I am better than Devaki's son, I am pleased with you."}},{"n":52,"text":"एष सारथ्यमातिष्ठे राधेयस्य यशस्विनः ।\nयुध्यतः पाण्डवाग्र्येण यथा त्वं वीर मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here I take up the charioteering of the glorious Radha's son as he fights the best of the Pandavas, as you think right, hero."}},{"n":53,"text":"समयश्च हि मे वीर कश्चिद्वैकर्तनं प्रति ।\nउत्सृजेयं यथाश्रद्धमहं वाचोऽस्य संनिधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I have one condition, hero, concerning Vikartana's son: that in his presence I may say what I like, as I choose.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":54,"text":"तथेति राजन्पुत्रस्ते सह कर्णेन भारत ।\nअब्रवीन्मद्रराजस्य सुतं भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So be it,\" said your son, O king, together with Karna, to the king of the Madras, O best of the Bharatas."}}]}]}